/Users/normy/autobyteus_org/autobyteus-worktrees/agent-team-hierarchical-handoffs/tickets/in-progress/agent-team-hierarchical-handoffs/requirements.md:232:- **R-053 — One AgentRun segment lifecycle authority and exact-turn ingress:** `AgentRun` shall own one non-persisted `AgentSegmentLifecycleState` and pass it through its existing per-run `AgentRunEventDispatchQueue` before every processor/listener. AutoByteus, Codex, and Claude adapters shall emit one minimal current source contract: `SEGMENT_START {id,turn_id,segment_type,metadata?}` establishes a finite `AgentSegmentType`; `SEGMENT_CONTENT {id,turn_id,delta}` and `SEGMENT_END {id,turn_id,...}` shall not repeat type. All segment IDs and turn IDs are non-empty; identity is exact `(AgentRun.runId,turn_id,id)`. AutoByteus shall retain its required handler/native turn; Claude shall use its session/projector-owned turn. Codex shall keep one pure `resolveCodexSegmentTurnAdmission` policy. Its production applicability and active-turn-inheritance set are the same exact four established segment-producing names: `item/started`, `item/agentMessage/delta`, `item/completed`, and `item/reasoning/completed`. `CodexThread.handleAppServerNotification()` shall invoke the resolver only for those four names, at the first per-thread native-notification boundary before `codex-thread-notification-handler.ts`, pending-MCP/item/reasoning mutation, locally derived emission, listener dispatch, converter entry, or raw event capture. Every other current item and non-item notification shall retain its existing operation-owned route without entering segment-turn admission and without a second exemption registry. The policy shall inspect every present candidate at `params.turn_id`, `params.turnId`, `params.item.turn_id`, `params.item.turnId`, and `params.turn.id`: every present field must be a non-empty string and all normalized values must equal the one current non-empty `CodexThread.activeTurnId`. Its stable inactive, explicit-invalid, conflicting, and unlisted-omission reason vocabulary remains unchanged; unlisted omission is an internal pure-policy misuse guard, not a supported provider event branch or a basis for runtime unknown-event machinery. A rejected governed candidate shall return at the thread boundary, produce zero provider-state change or emitted event, and record only `{runtimeKind,runId,nativeEventName,reasonCode}` without raw payload. An admitted governed result shall construct one immutable canonical thread notification containing `paramsWithExactTurn`; a non-governed current native fact shall be copied readonly at that same boundary without applying segment policy. `CodexThread` shall own an unexported brand plus the only private constructors/emitters for the closed `native_admitted | local_derived` listener value. The same branded value shall be the only input to notification handling and the listener/converter path; downstream code may import its opaque type but may not structurally manufacture or cast one. Locally derived notifications shall remain explicitly distinguished and may be constructed only by `CodexThread` from an admitted native fact or separately supported local operation. The converter shall not re-resolve, re-read raw params, accept a generic/direct-native bypass, or accept fabricated branded test input, and its admitted-event raw debugger shall run only after the first-boundary decision. A rejected normalization shall never reach `logRawCodexThreadEventDetails`, `appendRuntimeRawEventLog`, or a generic/raw payload fallback. Valid admitted MCP start/completion shall retain pending-state coordination and derived local completion, and valid admitted native/local events shall retain debug behavior over their accepted canonical values. Codex/Claude normalization shall emit explicit text/reasoning starts, reject unknown item kind/type instead of defaulting to text, and remain independent of Team code. The common transformer shall be the sole owner that correlates admitted